First, I should say that I believe sickness and stoning will normally 
kill you in polymorphed form - you don't return to your original form 
automatically.  Second, it may even be that if you return to it by a 
conscious polymorph they may not be cured.  They are cured, if you 
polymorph from doppelganger form to new doppelganger, however.  So two 
successive polymorphs would save you in that case.

Of course, you do lose power points on polymorphing (unless it is a 
return to doppelganger form from non-doppelganger).  In addition, each 
time you return to doppelganger form being killed in your polymorphed 
form you have only half your original Hp.  This will in many cases kick 
in before you cannot polymorph anymore due to lack of power. I don't 
know if it happens when you polymorph in sick form or in the 
slowing-down state.  But there the abusive potential is small, IMHO. 
Protection against stoning is easy to obtain by other means and sickness 
is a major problem only, if there are many repeated sickness attacks, 
like from Demogorgon (or Pestilence), in which case you can respond only 
a few times by polymorphing.  (Moreover, each time you polymorph to a 
new doppelganger form, your stats are randomly changed by a small 
amount, which I don't like once they are maxed out.)

Nevertheless, I think the conduct "you went without food" is not a real 
challenge for a doppelganger.  I like doppelgangers mostly because of 
their "liquid leap" technique, allowing an emergency escape (and also to 
save a lost Sokoban position, since you can leap past boulders by 
liquifying; I don't think there is a penalty to this).

